            <ArticleTitle>First confirmed record of Mola sp. A in the western Mediterranean Sea: morphological, molecular and parasitological findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1133-1141</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jfb.13247</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recent molecular and morphological studies suggest the existence of at least three species of Mola (Mola spp. A, B and C). Currently, only Mola mola and Mola ramsayi are formally accepted and species A, B or C have not been assigned to these thus far. In this study, a large ocean sunfish in the western Mediterranean Sea was analysed molecularly and morphologically, identified as Mola sp. A and a detailed account of the specimen's parasite load is reported.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 The Fisheries Society of the British Isles.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
